# M14: a Cut of more than the old 2,048-byte clipboard now works (CORE-44, CORE-230). The paragraph is 2,400 bytes: Select All and Cut take it
# whole onto the clipboard, Paste brings it back and one Edit > Undo takes the paste away again. (A copy too large for the 1 MB clipboard is
# still refused with "The document is too large for Quill." and changes nothing; the host test `clipboard.rs` covers that size.)
@copy bigsel.rtf
@open BIGSEL.RTF
f10 right l                     # Edit > Select All
f10 right t                     # Edit > Cut: the paragraph is on the clipboard and gone from the page
f10 right p                     # Edit > Paste: all 2,400 bytes are back
f10 right u                     # Edit > Undo: the paste goes, one step
f10 end enter                   # File > Exit
n                               # without saving
